# Styling, tokens, and CSS

Published runtime packages use **`rd-*` classnames** and **`--rd-*` custom properties** only. Builder app styling uses separate **`app-*`** BEM — never mix them in runtime code.

## Three styling modes (consumer choice)

| Mode | Import | Result |
|------|--------|--------|
| Minimal (default) | None | Structure, semantics, stable `rd-*` classnames; host styles everything |
| Tokenized | `@rosettadash/web-components/tokens.css` | `--rd-*` variables available; little component chrome |
| Themed | `@rosettadash/web-components/styles.css` (+ optional `tokens.css`) | Light borders/spacing using tokens |

Consumers override via CSS variables, `className`, and descendant selectors — no required Tailwind/MUI/CSS Modules peer dependency.

## Classname contract

| Piece | Pattern | Example |
|-------|---------|---------|
| Root block | `rd-<kebab>` | `rd-accordion`, `rd-chart-bar` |
| Element | `rd-<block>__<element>` | `rd-accordion__panel` |
| Modifier | `rd-<block>--<modifier>` | `rd-accordion--open` |

- Derive block from taxonomy: strip `visual.|domain.|layout.|logic.|infra.` prefix, dots → hyphens, prefix `rd-` (same as `taxonomyTypeToBemBlock()` in manifest).
- **`data-testid`** equals root block class.
- **No** generic `rd-atom` wrappers.

Custom element tags align with block where practical (`<rd-accordion>`).

## Tokens (`--rd-*`)

- **Public contract uses `--rd-*` only** — no `--db-*` in published CSS.
- Define shared tokens in `packages/web-components/src/styles/tokens.css`.
- Components read tokens with fallbacks: `var(--rd-color-border, #d0d0d0)`.
- **Never hard-code brand colors** in public component CSS — use tokens or `inherit`.

Common tokens (extend, do not rename without migration):

```css
--rd-color-text, --rd-color-muted, --rd-color-surface, --rd-color-border, --rd-color-accent
--rd-radius-sm, --rd-radius-md
--rd-space-xs, --rd-space-sm, --rd-space-md
--rd-font-size, --rd-line-height, --rd-font-family
```

## Drop-in rules (low opinionation)

1. **One job per component** — layout belongs to the host unless the atom *is* a layout primitive.
2. **No wrapper cards** unless the taxonomy component is explicitly a card (e.g. KPI).
3. **Recipes compose atoms** without inventing extra chrome.
4. **Width/height** default `auto` / `100%` of parent — no magic fixed widths.
5. **Stack styling profiles** (Tailwind, MUI, CSS Modules) are **export-wizard** choices — not runtime peerDeps.

## Library CSS prohibitions

Public `styles.css` must **not** include:

- Global `*` / `body` resets
- Fixed page layouts or app shells
- Heavy shadows, forced dark mode, or brand gradients
- Dependency on utility frameworks

## Accordion / collapsible open state

Panel **stays mounted** when closed; visibility via `rd-accordion--open` (or equivalent) + CSS.

If consumer skips `styles.css`, they **must** provide:

```css
.rd-accordion__panel { display: none; }
.rd-accordion--open .rd-accordion__panel { display: block; }
```

(Same pattern for `rd-collapsible`, `rd-modal-layout` where applicable.)

## Light DOM vs shadow DOM

| DOM | When | Styling |
|-----|------|---------|
| Light (default) | Native atoms via `RosettaAtomElement` | Host can target `rd-*` classes directly |
| Shadow | Manual media CEs only | Host styles via `--rd-*` on the CE + documented parts; frameworks pass `className` to host |

## Context matrix

| Context | Classes / tokens |
|---------|------------------|
| npm runtime packages | **Must** `rd-*` + `--rd-*` |
| Builder app | **Must** `app-*` (`docs/28-app-component-css-convention.md`) |
| Standalone export zip | May differ today; **new exporter work should converge on `rd-*` / `--rd-*`** |
| Proof apps | Use runtime package styling modes; app chrome may use stack choice |

## CE-host styling (React/Vue/Angular/Svelte)

- Merge `className` / `class` onto the custom element host.
- Pass `style` to host only.
- Tune internals via `--rd-*` variables on host or wrapper — do not pierce shadow DOM except via `setProperty`.

## Checklist

- [ ] Root uses taxonomy-aligned `rd-*` block
- [ ] No `--db-*` or hard-coded brand palette
- [ ] Themed mode uses tokens, not raw hex (except token defaults in `tokens.css`)
- [ ] Open/closed states use BEM modifiers, not inline `display:none` in TS
- [ ] No global resets added to `styles.css`

